data.reasoningText:
The `available` is `undefined` when `availableQuantity` is not set. Looking at the cart.ts code:

```typescript
const available = decision.availableQuantity;
if (!decision.available || (available !== undefined && available < line.quantity)) {
  throw new InventoryError(
    decision.reason ??
      `insufficient stock for ${line.product.id}: requested ${line.quantity}, available ${available ?? 0}`,
    line.product.id,
    line.quantity,
    available,  // <-- this is undefined when availableQuantity is not set
  );
```

When `availableQuantity` isn't provided, `available` gets passed to InventoryError as `undefined`, so I need to update the test to account for this.

